ts³11098020784³1version³13³1cache_oldmajor³10³1cache_oldauthor³10³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1revision³11³1tscreate³11098020784³1text_default³1ip³265.219.208.102³2ts³21098020784³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= What kind of hardware is supported by Linux? =

The answer is that most modern PC hardware is supported by Linux. However, there are certain pieces of hardware which may not work, so listed here are a variety of websites for you to check to make sure your hardware will be supported

1. General lists of compatible hardware.
:[http://www.mandrakelinux.com/en/hardware.php3 Mandrake Linux's List of Compatible Hardware]
:[http://hardware.redhat.com/hcl/ Redhat Linux's List of Compatible Hardware] 
:[http://www.tldp.org/HOWTO/Hardware-HOWTO/index.html Linux Hardware Compatibility HOWTO]
2. Help with Modems
:[http://linmodems.org/ LinModems.org]- Help finding Linux drivers for your modem.
3. Help with Wi-Fi cards
:[http://www.linux-wlan.org/ AbsoluteValue Systems] - Has a helpful FAQ and list of Linux-compatible Wi-Fi cards.
